From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:33:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/24] Document the durability decisions in the release notes
 and design docs

Release notes, header publication, compatibility rules, shared mode and
the connection string guide describe the new rules: a commit that cannot
be made durable throws before it writes, commits stay durable in the WAL
while only the data file cannot sync (with the header rule and the WAL
limit), failures are sticky with the engine read-only until reopened,
and durable commits=false is the way to use storage that cannot sync.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UFnsmor6qyZMSd1VoKwfJh
